TITLE:: SPOptions
summary:: the server's options, in ServerPanel's colours, applied when you say so
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/ServerOptions, Classes/ServerPanel, Classes/SPMeter

DESCRIPTION::
What ServerPanel's code::o:: key and its strong::Options:: entry open. Every link::Classes/ServerOptions:: setting worth changing, in cards by what it is about: the audio device (input and output device, sample rate, hardware buffer), the channels, what the server holds (real-time memory in MB, nodes, synthdefs, wire buffers, buffers, block size) and recording and timing (latency, record channels and formats). The rare ones fold under strong::more::.

A setting you change lights its name and waits. strong::apply:: sets the changes: latency and the recording settings belong to the server object and take effect at once; the rest are the server's options and take effect at its next boot, which the top row says. strong::apply and reboot:: does both, and reboots only when a change needs it. strong::revert:: forgets the changes, strong::defaults:: puts ServerOptions' own defaults in, to apply like any change. Hover over a setting and the hint bar says what it does.

One per server, like the scopes. It replaces ServerOptionsGui in the panel; that quark is still a dependency and works as before.

code::
SPOptions(s);
SPOptions(s).set(\memSize, 2 ** 17);   // as if changed in the window
SPOptions(s).apply;                     // or applyAndReboot
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
The options window of a server, opened if it is not.
ARGUMENT:: server
A link::Classes/Server::; code::Server.default:: when nil.
RETURNS:: an SPOptions

METHOD:: cards
What the window shows: an Array of [title, rows]; a row is [key, label, kind, extra, hint].

METHOD:: serverKeys
The settings that belong to the server object, not its options, and take effect at once.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: set
Change a setting, as if in the window: it waits for link::#-apply::.
ARGUMENT:: key
A ServerOptions setter's name without the underscore, or one of link::#*serverKeys::.
ARGUMENT:: value
The new value; the current one takes the change back.

METHOD:: valueOf
What a setting will be: the change waiting, or what it is now.
ARGUMENT:: key
The setting.

METHOD:: current
What a setting is now.
ARGUMENT:: key
The setting.

METHOD:: pending
The changes waiting, an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: of key -> value.

METHOD:: apply
Set the changes. The server's options take effect at its next boot.

METHOD:: applyAndReboot
Set the changes, and reboot the server if one of them needs it.

METHOD:: revert
Forget the changes.

METHOD:: defaults
Put ServerOptions' own defaults in, as changes waiting.

METHOD:: needsReboot
Whether a change waiting, once applied, needs a reboot to take effect.

METHOD:: front
Bring the window to the front.

METHOD:: close
Close the window. Changes not applied are forgotten.
